WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.120 --> 00:00:01.410
- I wanna finish things up

00:00:01.410 --> 00:00:03.030
with something particularly adorable

00:00:03.030 --> 00:00:04.170
that I found on social media.

00:00:04.170 --> 00:00:05.147
This is what I'm liking.

00:00:05.147 --> 00:00:08.310
(rock music)

00:00:08.310 --> 00:00:10.260
So you can never be exactly sure

00:00:10.260 --> 00:00:12.390
what you'll discover
in the pages of a book,

00:00:12.390 --> 00:00:13.590
and that's even more true

00:00:13.590 --> 00:00:15.870
if that book is checked
out from a library.

00:00:15.870 --> 00:00:17.190
Just look at some of the items

00:00:17.190 --> 00:00:20.220
an Oakland, California
librarian has come across

00:00:20.220 --> 00:00:22.350
in her 20 years on the job.

00:00:22.350 --> 00:00:25.890
So, everything from little
notes to recipes and receipts.

00:00:25.890 --> 00:00:28.028
Even a backstage concert pass.

00:00:28.028 --> 00:00:28.861
(audience laughing)

00:00:28.861 --> 00:00:30.780
Now she's helping reunite some readers

00:00:30.780 --> 00:00:31.980
with their lost relics

00:00:31.980 --> 00:00:34.530
with her Found in a Library Book project.

00:00:34.530 --> 00:00:35.640
We have her on the line right now.

00:00:35.640 --> 00:00:39.180
Everybody say hello to Sharon
watching on NBC Bay Area.

00:00:39.180 --> 00:00:40.326
What's up, Sharon?

00:00:40.326 --> 00:00:41.567
(audience clapping)

00:00:41.567 --> 00:00:43.560
- Hi, how are you?

00:00:43.560 --> 00:00:45.750
- Oh, you are so cute, by the way.

00:00:45.750 --> 00:00:47.400
How did this get started?

00:00:47.400 --> 00:00:49.260
- Oh, well, about 10 years ago

00:00:49.260 --> 00:00:51.690
I was put in charge of
the library's website

00:00:51.690 --> 00:00:53.934
and blogs were a big thing at that time.

00:00:53.934 --> 00:00:57.030
So, I was trying to come up
with something that was fun

00:00:57.030 --> 00:00:59.970
and would humanize the
library and library staff,

00:00:59.970 --> 00:01:02.820
and I had my own little
collection of things I'd found.

00:01:02.820 --> 00:01:05.670
So I reached out to library
staff around the system

00:01:05.670 --> 00:01:07.770
and asked them to send me
anything they had found

00:01:07.770 --> 00:01:10.110
and I turned that into a blog.

00:01:10.110 --> 00:01:12.450
I got like so many cool things.

00:01:12.450 --> 00:01:14.520
People leave all kinds of things in books.

00:01:14.520 --> 00:01:18.840
There's bookmarks,
postcards, notes and letters,

00:01:18.840 --> 00:01:23.840
kids drawings, a lot of
photos, a crochet hook even.

00:01:23.880 --> 00:01:27.690
So, each one is like a
tiny anonymous glimpse

00:01:27.690 --> 00:01:28.800
into somebody's life.

00:01:28.800 --> 00:01:30.780
I really, I really love that.

00:01:30.780 --> 00:01:34.530
So, last year we transitioned
to a different website

00:01:34.530 --> 00:01:37.410
and I was able to put up the full archive.

00:01:37.410 --> 00:01:40.200
And so, we have about 400 images up now,

00:01:40.200 --> 00:01:41.340
and I have several hundred more

00:01:41.340 --> 00:01:44.010
in a box under my desk waiting to go on.

00:01:44.010 --> 00:01:44.850
- This is super cool.

00:01:44.850 --> 00:01:46.440
So, you've found some really cool things

00:01:46.440 --> 00:01:48.750
and also, you've been
able to reunite people

00:01:48.750 --> 00:01:50.280
with their items, right?

00:01:50.280 --> 00:01:53.220
- Yeah, so I personally
love the kids' drawings.

00:01:53.220 --> 00:01:55.260
One of my favorites is a bookmark

00:01:55.260 --> 00:01:57.900
with a drawing of a robot
labeled "Robot Daddy,"

00:01:57.900 --> 00:01:59.280
and it has a speech bubble

00:01:59.280 --> 00:02:01.711
that says "Calculating I love beer."

00:02:01.711 --> 00:02:02.544
(Kelly laughing)

00:02:02.544 --> 00:02:05.040
There's also a really lovely postcard

00:02:05.040 --> 00:02:07.740
where a woman is writing to a man

00:02:07.740 --> 00:02:10.089
and expressing that she's
wishing him best wishes,

00:02:10.089 --> 00:02:11.820
even though he hasn't replied

00:02:11.820 --> 00:02:14.435
to her previous 30 some messages.

00:02:14.435 --> 00:02:15.268
- Oh.

00:02:15.268 --> 00:02:17.940
- Yeah, we have actually
been able to reunite a woman

00:02:17.940 --> 00:02:19.440
with some of her lost photos.

00:02:19.440 --> 00:02:21.464
She saw them and reached out to us.

00:02:21.464 --> 00:02:23.820
They were childhood
photos that had been lost

00:02:23.820 --> 00:02:26.130
because she moved around a lot as a child.

00:02:26.130 --> 00:02:28.020
She came and retrieved them.

00:02:28.020 --> 00:02:30.210
She's pregnant with her own baby

00:02:30.210 --> 00:02:32.670
and was so excited to have
these childhood photos

00:02:32.670 --> 00:02:34.380
of hers to share.

00:02:34.380 --> 00:02:35.820
- That is so cool.

00:02:35.820 --> 00:02:36.796
Look what you did.

00:02:36.796 --> 00:02:38.640
Even if just with a one person

00:02:38.640 --> 00:02:41.070
that's such a remarkably cool thing.

00:02:41.070 --> 00:02:42.210
Thank you so much, Sharon.

00:02:42.210 --> 00:02:43.980
I'm liking your post right now, all right.

00:02:43.980 --> 00:02:45.363
- [Sharon] Thank you.

00:02:46.320 --> 00:02:47.460
- And that's not all, ma'am.

00:02:47.460 --> 00:02:48.960
Our season long partner Pilot Pen,

00:02:48.960 --> 00:02:50.580
makers of FriXion, the go-to erasable pen

00:02:50.580 --> 00:02:51.900
of "The Kelly Clarkson Show,"

00:02:51.900 --> 00:02:53.910
want to celebrate those
creating fearlessly

00:02:53.910 --> 00:02:55.740
and promoting reading
just like you, ma'am.

00:02:55.740 --> 00:02:57.720
So, they're giving the nonprofit

00:02:57.720 --> 00:03:01.075
Friends of the Oakland
Public Library $1,000.

00:03:01.075 --> 00:03:02.328
(audience cheering)

00:03:02.328 --> 00:03:04.219
- Oh, that is so amazing!

00:03:04.219 --> 00:03:05.264
Thank you so much.

00:03:05.264 --> 00:03:06.608
- [Kelly] Absolutely.

00:03:06.608 --> 00:03:07.441
- [Sharon] That's awesome.

00:03:07.441 --> 00:03:08.274
- Thank you so much.

00:03:08.274 --> 00:03:10.110
And a big thanks to Kenneth
Babyface Edmonds, y'all,

00:03:10.110 --> 00:03:12.886
and Lawrence Zarian for
hanging out with us this hour.

00:03:12.886 --> 00:03:15.554
Y'all have a great day, and if
it's not, try and change it.

